# Shell scripts must check out with Unix line endings on every platform.
#
# CI executes tools/validate-skills.sh directly on Ubuntu, and bash refuses a
# script whose lines end in CRLF. Without this, a clone on Windows with the
# default core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF in the working tree and the script fails
# locally in a way that is hard to recognise from the error.
*.sh text eol=lf
